  "prefLabel": "Ch 501.01 Obligation to Obey",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ch 501.01 Obligation to Obey.\n\n(a) The ethical standards set forth in this part shall bind all licensees and those with the privilege to practice, and violation of any such standard shall constitute unprofessional conduct.\n\n(b) Conduct proscribed by these ethical standards, when performed by an unlicensed person or during a prior period of licensure, shall also be a basis for denying an application for licensure or constitute misconduct subject to disciplinary action.\n\nSource. #4671, eff 9-7-89; ss by #5624, eff 5-18-93, EXPIRED: 5-18-99\n\nNew. #14143, eff 12-16-24, EXPIRES: 12-16-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ch100-500.html"
